> But how would "(n+1.3)^(3.15*r^2)" be expressed under this new xorxe's
> proposal then?
>

The proposal is not at all new, it is quite ancient.

That expression does not involve any mixed digit/lerfu string, therefore
the proposal does not affect it. It involves two one-lerfu strings: "n" and
"r", and 3 PA-only strings "1.3", "3.15" and "2". No mixed strings.

